PhoneValidator
==============

Strict validation for phone numbers in the US, Canada, and Australia.

Installation
============

Add the gem to your Gemfile:

  gem "validation_kit"

Usage
=====

class Person < ActiveRecord::Base
  validates :phone, phone: { country: "US", set: true }, allow_blank: true
end

There are three ways to specify the country. Country codes are
case-insensitive ("CA", "ca", or :CA).

 (1) Pass the country code as a string:

  validates :phone, phone: { country: "CA" }

 (2) Pass the name of a method on your model that returns the country code:

  validates :phone, phone: { country: :billing_country }

 (3) Leave it out, and the validator calls your model's country method:

  validates :phone, phone: true

Validation is skipped when the country isn't supported.

Options
=======

  set: true       Reformat the stored value, e.g. "1-212-555-1234 x5"
                  becomes "(212) 555-1234 x5" and "0298765432" becomes
                  "(02) 9876 5432".
  area_key: "VIC" For Australian landlines entered without an area code, the
                  state whose area code to add (default NSW/ACT, 02).
  message: "..."  A custom error message. Otherwise the standard :invalid
                  error is added; translate it with
                  activerecord.errors.models.person.attributes.phone.invalid.

Supported countries are Canada (CA), the United States (US) and Australia (AU).


